-- Row il-44. EXPECTED RED: the one defect, D1, kept as assertions that FAIL. The count is 2, declared in check.sh and in encoding.json `expected_red`.
-- Both would pass if section 12A1(a)(2)(b) read "to the Criminal Procedure Ordinance" where it reads "to the Criminal Procedure Law". A failing assertion here is the finding, not a mistake of the test.
-- Do not change an expected value to make either pass.

§ `D1: section 32 of the Criminal Procedure Law`

-- Red 1: the words say the vehicle was seized under a power to seize; section 32 of the Law has no text, so the citation does not point at what it says.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` `reference D1: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 32, as written`

-- Red 2: paragraph (1) of the same subsection names the Ordinance for section 32, and (2)(b) names the Law for the same number.
#ASSERT `the two citations name the same instrument for the same section number` `reference D1: 12A1(a)(2)(b) to section 32, as written` `reference C1: 12A1(a)(1) to section 32 of the Ordinance`
